	<text xml:lang="la">
		<body>
			<div xml:id="div1" corresp="regest1">
				<p>
					<s n="1" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z2"/>S.</s>
					<s n="2" xml:lang="la">Non me recte accusas negligentię, mi <persName ref="p495">Bullingere</persName>; nam eo die, quo postremas tuas<note xml:id="fn1" type="footnote" n="1">Nicht erhalten.</note> <lb xml:id="p1z3"/>scripsisti, et ego meas<note xml:id="fn2" type="footnote" n="2">Oben <ref target="file11831">Nr. 1785</ref>.</note> ferendas ad te commendavi (quamvis descriptas a <persName ref="p1550">Leodegario</persName><note xml:id="fn3" type="footnote" n="3"><persName ref="p1550">Leodegar Hirsgarter</persName> (vgl. ebd., Anm. a). Über ihn vermerkt <persName ref="p495">Bullinger</persName> in seiner Stipendiatenliste: "Was ein geflißner, geschickter mensch, der vil und wol schreib" (Zürich ZB, Ms Car C 44, 922, Nr. 22).</note> tuo) <lb xml:id="p1z4"/>per parochum vici ditionis istius <placeName ref="l1244">Wald</placeName><note xml:id="fn4" type="footnote" n="4">Pfarrer <persName ref="p5750">Martin Manhart</persName> aus <placeName ref="l1244">Wald</placeName> war zwecks Eheschließung nach <placeName ref="l28">Basel</placeName> gereist, wie sich einem Brief <persName ref="p8171">Theodor Biblianders</persName> an <persName ref="p8418">Myconius</persName> entnehmen lässt; s. Zürich StA, E II 340, 60.</note>.</s>
					<s n="3" xml:lang="la">Si<pb type="edition" next="271"/> nihil<note xml:id="fna" type="footnote" n="a">nihil <hi>am Rande nachgetragen.</hi></note> reddidit, requirito; nam omnia, quę novi certa, <lb xml:id="p1z5"/>misi.</s>
					<s n="4" xml:lang="la">Pręterea de <persName ref="p8462">Coloniensi</persName><note xml:id="fn5" type="footnote" n="5">Erzbischof <persName ref="p8462">Hermann von Wied</persName>.</note> quędam significarat <persName ref="p467">Bucerus</persName>,<note xml:id="fn6" type="footnote" n="6"><persName ref="p467">Bucer</persName> an <persName ref="p8418">Myconius</persName>, 26. September 1543 (Zürich ZB, Ms F 80, 175).</note> quę continui, quia noram <persName ref="p467">Bucerum</persName> <lb xml:id="p1z6"/>ipsum scripsisse tibi per <persName ref="p4851">Froschouerum</persName><note xml:id="fn7" type="footnote" n="7"><persName ref="p467">Bucer</persName> hatte im erwähnten Brief an <persName ref="p8418">Myconius</persName> angekündigt, durch <persName ref="p4851">Froschauer</persName> an <persName ref="p495">Bullinger</persName> schreiben zu wollen; der Brief an <persName ref="p495">Bullinger</persName> datiert vom 26. September (oben <ref target="file11835">Nr. 1789</ref>).</note> longe plura, quem nescio tamen, an redierit.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="5" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z7"/>Tribus agminibus proficiscitur <persName ref="p18538">cęsar</persName><note xml:id="fn8" type="footnote" n="8"><persName ref="p18538">Karl V.</persName></note> in <persName ref="p20225">Gallum</persName><note xml:id="fn9" type="footnote" n="9">König <persName ref="p20225">Franz I.</persName> von <placeName ref="l832">Frankreich</placeName>.</note>, qui pleraque oppida in d[itione] <placeName ref="l39">Lutzenburgensi</placeName> cepit <lb xml:id="p1z8"/>et incendit, nuper etiam <placeName ref="l39">Lutzenburgum</placeName> ipsum<note xml:id="fn10" type="footnote" n="10">Die Hauptstadt des Herzogtums war am 12. September erobert worden. Zum Vormarsch der <placeName ref="l832">französischen</placeName> Truppen und zum Beginn der Gegenoffensive des Kaisers s. <bibl source="b301">Henne</bibl> VIII 133-138.</note>.</s>
					<s n="6" xml:lang="la">Superest <placeName ref="l1922">Diedenhofen</placeName><note xml:id="fn11" type="footnote" n="11"><placeName ref="l1922">Thionville</placeName> (<placeName ref="l3216">Dép. Moselle</placeName>).</note>, quod oppidum si oc<lb xml:id="p1z9"/>cuparit, in ea regione negocium erit cęsari.</s>
					<s n="7" xml:lang="la"><placeName ref="l875">Hispanis</placeName> et <placeName ref="l834">Italis</placeName><note xml:id="fn12" type="footnote" n="12">Gemeint sind kaiserliche Soldaten.</note> nihil pertinaciter malignius.</s>
					<s n="8" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z10"/>Dum transierunt per ditionem <persName ref="p8462">Coloniensis</persName>, hic clamor fuit: „Maza, maza Lutheran[os?]<note xml:id="fnb" type="footnote" n="b"><hi>In der Vorlage</hi> Lutherân.</note>!“<note xml:id="fn13" type="footnote" n="13">Etwa im Sinne von: "Tötet die Lutheraner", vgl. den <placeName ref="l834">italienischen</placeName> Kriegsruf "Ammazza, ammazza!" (s. Salvatore <hi>Battaglia,</hi> Grande dizionario della lingua italiana, Bd. I. Turin 1961, S. 403).</note></s>
					<s n="9" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z11"/>Vastarunt omnia, pepercerunt hominibus tamen.</s>
					<s n="10" xml:lang="la">Ex mandato, quod mittit <persName ref="p1278">Gastius</persName>,<note xml:id="fn14" type="footnote" n="14">Nämlich das Mandat gegen Bürgermeister und Rat von <placeName ref="l1875">Hildesheim</placeName>, s. oben <ref target="file11837">Nr. 1791</ref>, 13f mit Anm. 8.</note> videbis impietatem <lb xml:id="p1z12"/>cęsaris.</s>
					<s n="11" xml:lang="la">Quamvis d[ominus] et amicus noster de <persName ref="p7730">Rischach</persName><note xml:id="fn15" type="footnote" n="15"><persName ref="p7730">Ludwig von Reischach</persName>.</note> mirabiliter hunc tueatur.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="12" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z13"/>Scripserat insuper M. <persName ref="p5957">Theobaldus Nigri</persName><note xml:id="fn16" type="footnote" n="16">Ein entsprechender Brief liegt nicht vor.</note> et <placeName ref="l260">Cracoviam</placeName> obsessam a <persName ref="p18593">Turca</persName><note xml:id="fn17" type="footnote" n="17">Sultan <persName ref="p18593">Suleiman I.</persName></note>.</s>
					<s n="13" xml:lang="la">Equidem <lb xml:id="p1z14"/>spero meliora.</s>
					<s n="14" xml:lang="la">Ea<note xml:id="fnc" type="footnote" n="c"><hi>Vor</hi> Ea <hi>ein gestrichener Buchstabe.</hi></note> re terribilius nihil; nam sine negocio foret illa occupata aditus <lb xml:id="p1z15"/>in <placeName ref="l749">Saxoniam</placeName>.</s>
					<s n="15" xml:lang="la">Et circumfertur libellus de proditione <placeName ref="l834">Italorum</placeName> quorundam contra <placeName ref="l1931">Strigonium</placeName><note xml:id="fn18" type="footnote" n="18">Zur Flugschrift über die Eroberung von <placeName ref="l1931">Gran</placeName> s. oben <ref target="file11834">Nr. 1788</ref>, 271 mit Anm. 32.</note>.</s>
					<s n="16" xml:lang="la">Captum <lb xml:id="p1z16"/>adserunt et <placeName ref="l1895">Stuͦlwissenburg</placeName><note xml:id="fn19" type="footnote" n="19">Zur Einnahme von <placeName ref="l1895">Stuhlweißenburg (Székesfehérvár, Ungarn)</placeName> durch die <placeName ref="l2510">Türken</placeName> am 4. September s. <persName ref="p4958">Paulo Giovio</persName>, Historiae sui temporis II/2, Rom 1985. -Opera V, S. 145-154; <bibl source="b276">Hammer-Purgstall</bibl> III 259.</note>.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="17" xml:lang="la">Hęc sunt tempora praesentia.</s>
					<s n="18" xml:lang="la">Dominus tueatur verbum suum.</s>
					<s n="19" xml:lang="la" ana="farewell"><lb xml:id="p1z17"/>Vale.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="20" xml:lang="la"><placeName ref="l28">Basileę</placeName>, kalendis octobris anno 1543.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="21" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z18"/><persName ref="p8418">Os. Myconius</persName> <lb xml:id="p1z19"/>tuus.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<note type="address">[Adresse auf der Rückseite:]</note>
					<s n="22" xml:lang="la"><pb/><lb xml:id="p2z1"/>D. <persName ref="p495">Heinricho Bullingero</persName> <lb xml:id="p2z2"/>doctissimo suo.</s>
				</p>
